  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to TAHA: Growing Wealth Through Horticulture (GROWTH) - Support to TAHA -Growing Wealth Through Horticulture (GROWTH)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Support to TAHA: Growing Wealth Through Horticulture (GROWTH)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution aims to contribute to increased commercial&#xa0;competitiveness and sustainability of the horticultural sector in Tanzania. The Swedish support is directed to the non-profit Association (TAHA) through the project &apos;Growing Wealth through Horticulture&apos;. The focus is to increase knowledge on sustainable and climate resilient&#xa0;farming methods and increases&#xa0;economic gains through improved marketing and trade facilitation.&#xa0;

Using market systems development approach, the project&#xa0; works with actors at all levels of the horticulture value chain, namely: input suppliers, producers, processors, logistics service providers, traders, and consumers. In addition, the project work with value chain supporting institutions such as finance, quality and standards accreditation institutions and providers of entrepreneurship services. &#xa0;&#xa0;A range of demand-driven horticultural crops are currently grown and can be cultivated in the various agro-ecological zones/regions. TAHA is therefore continuing to establish tailored information systems to link producers on supply side and the demand side with the required standards for a diverse range of horticultural products in the domestic, East African region, Southern Africa, Europe and Middle Eastern areas.&#xa0;

Analysis and advocacy for better policy and business regulatory environment is an important pillar of the intervention to attract investment and trade. The outcome results of the project includes increased opportunities for jobs and incomes at micro level and increase in sector&apos;s contribution to economic growth. The expected impact of the the intervention is the contribution of the sector in alleviation of income /resource and other dimensions of Poverty. The project also contribute to creating awareness on improved nutrition and gender integration</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektets &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att &#xf6;ka konkurrenskraft och h&#xe5;llbarhet f&#xf6;r hortikultur (tr&#xe4;dg&#xe5;rdsodling).  Det svenska st&#xf6;det riktas till den ideella organisationen (TAHA) genom projektet &quot;Growing Wealth through Horticulture&quot; med fokus p&#xe5;:
&#x2022; &#xd6;ka produktiviteten genom att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra kunskap om effektiva och h&#xe5;llbara jordbruksmetoder, med tonvikt p&#xe5; att integrera milj&#xf6; och klimatf&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar,
&#x2022; &#xd6;ka tillg&#xe5;ngen till marknader f&#xf6;r tanzaniska hortikultur produkter,
&#x2022; Bidra till opinionsbildning och fr&#xe4;mjande av en b&#xe4;ttre politik och aff&#xe4;rsm&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;rande milj&#xf6; f&#xf6;r hortikulturens konkurrenskraft och delaktighet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective (s) of the Project is increasing competitiveness and sustainability of horticultural industry.  The Swedish support is directed to the non-profit Association (TAHA) through the project &quot;Growing Wealth through Horticulture&quot; with focus on:  
&#x2022; Increasing productivity by improved 
 knowledge on efficient and sustainable farming methods, with emphasis on integrating environment and climate change , 
&#x2022; increase access to markets for Tanzanian horticultural products, 
&#x2022; Contributing to advocacy for better policy and business enabling environment for horticultural industry&apos;s competitiveness and inclusiveness.</narrative>
  </description>
